        "original_id": "39a05019-dabe-59e6-9910-1fbe78dfc6bd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Fenwick, Northumberland; Bamburgh; Northumberland; Farne Islands\n- Landmarks: Lindisfarne Castle; Bamburgh Castle; Chillingham Castle\n- People: Sir Claudius Forster, 1st Baronet\n- Roles: Governors of Bamburgh Castle\n\nFacts:\n- In 1609, Sir Claudius Forster, 1st Baronet, was granted ownership of Bamburgh Castle and its estates by the Crown.\n- Sir Claudius Forster, 1st Baronet, was descended from a long line of Governors of Bamburgh Castle.\n- Bamburgh Castle is on the northeast coast of England by the village of Bamburgh in Northumberland.\n- Fenwick, Northumberland, is close to Lindisfarne Castle, Bamburgh Castle, and Chillingham Castle.\n- Fenwick, Northumberland, is an ideal base for exploring the history of Northumberland and the Farne Islands.",
